by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-01T13:31:56Z

Thanks @recchia. I rebased on 8.2, squashed the six commits into one, and pushed the following changes on top.

**Missing split package.** `splitsh.json` listed 82 of the 83 notifier bridge directories; `WhatsApp` was
the only one absent, so `symfony/whats-app-notifier` would never have been published while both
`UnsupportedSchemeException` and `FrameworkExtension` tell users to require it. Added the entry.

**Exception contract.** `doSend()` called `$response->toArray(false)` unconditionally, before the status
check. A non-JSON body, such as a proxy's HTML 502 page or a 200 with an empty body, escaped as
`HttpClient\Exception\JsonException`, which does not implement `Notifier\Exception\TransportExceptionInterface`,
the only exception `TransportInterface::send()` documents. The decode now happens inside the failure
branch and falls back to `getContent(false)`, and the success decode is guarded too. Both shapes are
covered by tests.

**`supports()`.** It returned `true` for a bare `ChatMessage`, but `doSend()` always throws for one since
there is no DSN-level default recipient. In a chatter with several transports, WhatsApp claimed
messages it could not deliver and they never reached a transport that could. It now requires a
resolvable recipient, via the existing `ChatMessage::getRecipientId()`.

**Test coverage.** Three mutations survived the original 24-test suite: dropping `messaging_product`
(a required Cloud API field), dropping `recipient_type`, and replacing `auth_bearer` with an arbitrary
header, which left the authentication entirely unasserted. All three are now asserted on the outgoing
request and are caught.

**API version.** `DEFAULT_API_VERSION` was `v21.0`, released October 2024 and due to expire in January
2027, before 8.2 reaches end of life. Bumped to `v26.0`, the current Graph API version. Still
overridable with `?api_version=`.

**Smaller items.** Fixed the `phpunit.xml.dist` test suite name, which still carried the old bridge
name; dropped the README claim that the `Vonage` bridge supports WhatsApp, since it has no WhatsApp
handling at all, and pointed at `Twilio` instead; removed two em-dashes; relaxed the
`recipientPhoneNumber()` docblock, which claimed digits only although Meta accepts a leading `+` and
nothing normalized it; added `WhatsAppOptions::getTemplate()` in place of reaching into `toArray()`.

A DSN-level default recipient looks like a reasonable follow-up but is out of scope here, and is
noted as such in the description.

@alexandre-daubois your review is fully addressed: `Transport::FACTORY_CLASSES`,
`UnsupportedSchemeException::SCHEME_TO_PACKAGE_MAP` and its test provider are all wired up, so it can
be resolved.

Bridge suite is at 28 tests, 49 assertions. `src/Symfony/Component/Notifier/Tests` passes with 185
tests, 347 assertions.
